# Downloaded guideline corpus: re-fetchable from a stable PMCID, and keeping
# third-party guideline text out of git history avoids any redistribution
# question (DEV_PLAN risk #5).
corpus/
# Segmenter output: generated, large, and full of verbatim source text.
*.jsonl
# EXCEPT the replay cassettes. These are the reproducibility artefact --
# test_replay.py runs the full pipeline against a real recorded run with no API
# key -- and they do NOT carry the redistribution risk the rule above is about:
# the prompt is stored as a SHA-256 hash rather than as text, so the source
# document cannot be reconstructed from a tape. What remains is a section
# breadcrumb and the model's response, i.e. individual quoted recommendation
# sentences from open-access articles. ~84 KB for both.
!cassettes/*.jsonl
__pycache__/
